<newsitem itemid="190241" id="root" date="1996-11-14" xml:lang="en">
<title>FINLAND: Nokia 9-mth pre-tax profit FIM 2,228 mln.</title>
<headline>Nokia 9-mth pre-tax profit FIM 2,228 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to end-Sept 1996-</p>
<p>					   (million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit before tax, minority interest     2,228 vs 3,984</p>
<p> Earnings per share (markka)		   5.70 vs 10.50</p>
<p> Net sales					 26,652 vs 25,855</p>
<p> Operating profit				 2,529 vs 3,993</p>
<p>NOTE - Median forecast by 19 analysts for Finnish telecoms group Nokia's January-September profit before tax and minorities was 2,198 million markka (range 2,010-2,427 million).  </p>
<p> Cost of goods sold			    19,352 vs 17,658</p>
<p> Research and development expenses	  2,453 vs 1,825</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>  administrative expenses		     2,318 vs 2,379</p>
<p> Share of results of associated companies    51 vs 69</p>
<p> Net financial expenses			   352 vs 78</p>
<p> Taxes						  595 vs 940</p>
<p> Minorities				   charge 15 vs 57 charge</p>
<p> Profit from continuing operations	  1,618 vs 2,987</p>
<p> Discontinued operations			  nil vs 216 charge</p>
<p>Profit from ordinary activities before</p>
<p>cumulative effect of change in</p>
<p>  accounting policies			   1,618 vs 2,771</p>
<p>Cumulative prior year effect (after tax)</p>
<p>  of change in accounting policies	    nil vs 485</p>
<p> Net profit					 1,618 vs 3,256</p>
<p>NOTE - Company's full name is Nokia Oy.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +35 80 6805 0245</p>
</text>
